<title>UK: OKB sets 10 billion yen dual-currency 3-year bond.</title>
<headline>OKB sets 10 billion yen dual-currency 3-year bond.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following bond was announced by lead manager Citibank International.</p>
<p> BORROWER   OESTERREICHISCHE KONTROLLBANK</p>
<p> GUARANTOR  REPUBLIC OF AUSTRIA</p>
<p> AMT    10 BLN YEN    COUPON     4.70 PCT  MATURITY    27.JAN.00</p>
<p> TYPE	 STRAIGHT  ISS PRICE  100.0     PAY DATE    27.JAN.97</p>
<p> FULL FEES  1.75	DENOMS (K) 500	 SALE LIMITS US/UK</p>
<p> MOODY/S&amp;P  AAA/AAA   LISTING    =	   PAY FREQ    SEMI-ANN</p>
<p> GOV LAW    ENGLISH   HOME CTRY  AUSTRIA   FORCE MAJ   YES</p>
<p> NOTES	ISSUED UNDER THE EUROSHELF FOR ISSUES OF DEBT</p>
<p>		SECURITIES</p>
<p>		REDEMPTION PRICE $4,291.85 PER 500,000 YEN</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
</text>
